// src/v4/std/witness.dag
//
// Scope: fail-closed read discipline — no Option::None in lens reads.
// Anchor: THESIS fail-closed discipline + INVARIANTS P3 (no Option::None in lens reads)
//
// Owns:
//   - Witness<C> = Holds(C) | Violates(diagnostic: Diagnostic)
//     (Holds CARRIES the proven fact C; Violates CARRIES the full
//     Diagnostic. A successful read must compose its result forward — a
//     payload-less success variant would silently drop the fact it
//     proved, violating facts-flow-forward / INVARIANTS P2 and re-
//     importing the Option::None hole this type exists to close. The
//     failure arm is symmetric: a bare reason tag would drop the `at`
//     locus and `correction` the failing read already knows — so
//     Violates carries the whole Diagnostic, not a name-reference.)
//   - replaces Option::None at lens read channels
//
// Consumes:
//   - std/node.dag: Disj for sum
//   - std/diagnostic.dag: Diagnostic (the Violates payload)
//
// Status: T-3 modeled 2026-05-16 (quiet-deer-32).
//
// HEADER RECONCILE (operator-ratified Option A, 2026-05-16). The original
// scaffold header declared `Violates(reason: NamedReason)`, consuming
// `std/diagnostic.dag: NamedReason`. PR #3161 deleted `NamedReason` from
// diagnostic.dag — its `reason` is now an opaque `Symbol` name-reference,
// and the diagnostic.dag fail-closed error type is `Diagnostic`. This
// session STOP'd on the dangling contract; the operator ratified Option
// A — `Violates` carries the full `Diagnostic` (reason + at + correction),
// not a bare reason tag. The `Owns` and `Consumes` lines above reflect
// that ratified reconcile; no other scaffold-header content changed.


module v4.std.witness


import v4.std.diagnostic { Diagnostic }


// ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
// Modeling notes (read before validating against the anchor)
//
// SCHEMA FILE. witness.dag declares one type — the fail-closed proof
// carrier `Witness<C>`. Like std/diagnostic.dag it owns no producer
// logic: the lenses (T-12 cost … T-21 affected-set) and every other
// fallible structural read CONSTRUCT `Witness<C>` values; this file is
// the shape they construct to. There is deliberately no `witness_holds`
// predicate and no unwrap helper — a consumer reads a `Witness` by
// `match`, handling BOTH arms (INVARIANTS P3); a helper that returned
// the held `C` alone would re-open the silent-drop path this type
// exists to close.
//
// WHY A WITNESS AND NOT `Option<C>`. A fallible read either proves a
// fact or it does not. `Option<C>` collapses "proved nothing" and
// "failed to prove" into one `None` and carries no reason — the exact
// INVARIANTS P3 violation (no Option::None in lens reads). `Witness<C>`
// splits the two: `Holds` carries the proven `C` forward (facts-flow-
// forward), and `Violates` carries a full `Diagnostic` — reason + locus
// + correction — so a failed read is a *helpful* failure (CULTURE §5
// no-engine), never a bare absence.
//
// The coproduct below carries the full Practice-4 🟢/🟡/🔴
// classification + the five-pattern dissolution ledger (modeling-
// discipline.md §4 — operator-ratified binding 2026-05-15; the doc
// enumerates FIVE patterns, the fifth being Parameterized-family).


// ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
// Witness<C> — the fail-closed proof carrier (THESIS fail-closed
// discipline, INVARIANTS P3). The result of every structural read that
// can fail: it either HOLDS the proven fact or REPORTS a violation.
// There is no "probably fine" — CULTURE §2.
//
//   - Holds carries the proven fact `C` itself. A read that succeeded
//     KNOWS something, and that knowledge must compose forward (facts-
//     flow-forward / INVARIANTS P2). A payload-less `Holds` would
//     silently drop the proven fact — re-importing the Option::None
//     hole this type exists to close.
//   - Violates carries a full `Diagnostic` (reason + `at` locus +
//     `correction`). The failure arm is symmetric to `Holds`: the read
//     that failed also KNOWS something — where it failed, and often the
//     fix — and that must flow forward too. A bare reason tag would
//     drop the locus and correction, the failure-side facts-drop. Per
//     operator-ratified Option A (2026-05-16) the payload is the whole
//     `Diagnostic`, std/diagnostic.dag's fail-closed error type.
//
// Coproduct dissolution (Practice 4 / INVARIANTS P1 / modeling-
// discipline.md §4) — classification: 🟢 GREEN (terminal). Ledger —
// five patterns attempted:
//   1. Fact placement — FAILS: every witness consumer (every fallible
//      lens read site) handles BOTH arms — compose the proven `C`
//      forward, or surface the `Diagnostic`. It is the shared read-
//      channel result, not a per-consumer scattered fact.
//   2. Variant-is-data — FAILS: the arms carry DIFFERENT shapes (the
//      proven fact `C`; a `Diagnostic`). Collapsing to a flat
//      `{ held: Bool, value?: C, diagnostic?: Diagnostic }` record
//      makes `held: true` with no `value` (and `held: false` with no
//      `diagnostic`) representable — that IS the Option::None hole this
//      type exists to close (the inverse of P2).
//   3. Algebraic form — N/A by construction: `Witness<C>` is the fail-
//      closed read-channel primitive itself; it is not the carrier of a
//      richer std/algebra.dag structure (there is no Monoid/Group it
//      inhabits), and the held/violated dichotomy traces to no richer
//      std/ source.
//   4. Dimensional — FAILS: a read EITHER held a proof OR reported a
//      violation — mutually-exclusive outcomes, never simultaneous
//      coordinates. No witness is "both held and violated".
//   5. Parameterized family — FAILS: the two variants are not `F<X>`
//      over a declared set. `Holds` carries the type parameter `C` (the
//      proven fact); `Violates` carries a `Diagnostic` — structurally
//      distinct payloads, not a mechanical copy of an enumerable set
//      (not a Practice-7 projection). `Witness<C>`'s own genericity
//      over `C` is the genuine proven-fact parameter, not an
//      enumerated-copy smell.
// Terminal: the irreducible two-case fail-closed proof carrier — held
// proof vs reported violation, the success/failure dichotomy at every
// fallible read channel. The sum IS the dissolved form of the
// "boolean + two optionals" shape pattern 2 rejects.
type Witness<C>
  = Holds { value: C }
  | Violates { diagnostic: Diagnostic }

